WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:05.658
What distinguishes Indian food is its magical use of spices.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.850
I always loved food.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.820
And what I perhaps didn't know is

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.730
that I had a very good palate because everything

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.584
that I was eating as a child, I somehow recorded.

00:00:19.626 --> 00:00:21.630
India is a vast country.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.700
It's the size of Europe.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.360
And this variety of food that we have

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.590
is what makes Indian food Indian, not curry.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.810
I don't think we had such
a word until the British came to India.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.510
It stood in their mind for all Indian food.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.901
How can you take all that food and call it all curry?

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.280
If you know nothing about Indian food,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.590
you take this class just to learn.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.780
Isn't it fun to find out what they

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.060
do in other parts of the world?

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.820
I'm going to talk about spices.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.610
Nobody knows spices like we do.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.470
We are masters.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.200
I will show you how to make Indian breads,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.970
how to cook a lot of the vegetables.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:08.010
And meats.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.080
Then we'll make street food.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:16.820
I often serve this as my first course to get the juices going.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.600
It's just delicious.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.030
When you cook rice, each grain should

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:24.600
be like brothers, close to each other, but not stuck

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.530
to each other.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.740
I call mustard seeds the Jekyll and Hyde of spices.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.710
They can be very spicy and pungent and hot

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:36.490
or, if you pop them in hot oil, they turn sweet and nutty.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.790
Eating is such an important part of our lives.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.880
It really tells you who you are in many ways.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.960
What you eat, how you eat it, what your culinary traditions

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.470
are tells me a lot about the people of that country.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:55.960
So if you want to know what 1.4 billion people are doing

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:00.100
with their lives, how they live, come, watch this class,

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.459
and you'll get a good idea.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:06.562
I'm Madhur Jaffrey, and this is MasterClass.

